But note: the "pump" in the CAD is a dark teal bag. Good.

Hero: a custom SVG schematic would be more editorial/convincing. Given time (02:34, budget to 02:41:42), I'll build the page with an SVG hero illustration (labeled "Ilustración conceptual") + CAD images in section 3 labeled as CAD P2.04 views. Copy the 3 PNGs into the new web folder as assets.

Structure: single index.html with inline CSS/JS (simple, no deps), assets/ folder with 3 PNGs + favicon maybe. Sections: portada, desafío, propuesta, IMU, validación, cierre. Sticky nav with mobile menu, smooth scroll, reveal animations respecting prefers-reduced-motion, IMU chart as inline SVG labeled "ejemplo ilustrativo".

Let me check IMU docs quickly? Brief says consult IMU documentation briefly. There's a grep result only in skills. Let me grep for "IMU" in the project docs (ESTADO_ACTUAL mentions?). Quick grep raw.

Time is tight. Do one quick grep combined with asset creation.

Plan the palette: 
--ink #1a1c1a (grafito), --paper #f5f2ea (blanco cálido), --yellow #f2c200 / safety #ffc400, --muted.

Typography: system stack with fallback; use Georgia for display? "editorial product tech": use a strong sans (Inter unavailable offline) — use "Helvetica Neue", Arial. For display, maybe use 'Georgia', serif for contrast? I'd rather do a big tight sans display. Keep it system-only (no external deps permitted — no network fonts).

Let me write index.html now, comprehensively but efficiently. Also copy images.

Content facts to use (verifiable):
- Bomba: mochila flexible Scotty (agua), no rígida.
- Estructura: 2 canales de aluminio 6061-T6, 32×28... use P2.04: canal 32×24×3. Masa rígida 1,44 kg; presupuesto auxiliar 2,21 kg sin bomba ni agua; arnés/textiles reserva 0,65 kg.
- Espaldera HDPE 1 mm, cunas textiles, cinturón, correas.
- IMU: registro de orientación/inclinación; no miden fuerza ni presión.
- Validación pendiente: mediciones de bomba, CdG, reparto, FEA, ensayos, fatiga, ergonomía.

Numbers as "modelo" not results. Fine — labeling as prediseño.

Write files now. I'll do 3 files: index.html, README.md, assets/*.png (copied). Maybe styles inline to save time (allowed: "HTML, CSS y JavaScript sencillos"). I'll use external styles.css + app.js for editability — the brief asks "archivos editables". Yes: index.html, styles.css, app.js.

Let me write CSS first (long), then HTML, then JS. Keep efficient but polished.

Given time, I'll write index.html with full content and link CSS/JS.

Hero SVG: draw a schematic: firefighter silhouette back view (simple geometric shapes), packed pump (rounded bag with water level), two aluminium rails, lumbar plate, belt, shoulder straps, plus dimension callouts and label "Ilustración conceptual". Do it inline in the hero as an SVG with layered shapes — must look good. Keep it geometric/editorial: dark graphite bg, yellow accents, thin light lines.

I'll build the SVG carefully but not too complex: 
- viewBox 0 0 700 760.
- Back figure: head circle, torso path (shoulders), arms, hips — semi-abstract outline in pale color.
- Pump: rounded rect bag behind shoulders with a water fill (teal-blue translucent) + valve.
- Rails: two vertical rounded rects with slots.
- Lumbar plate + belt band with buckle.
- Straps crossing diagonally.
- Callout dots + labels with leader lines: "Bomba flexible", "Estructura 6061-T6", "Cunas textiles", "Cinturón", "Correas".

To keep it clean: put the figure head/torso as a subtle silhouette behind, and label with small caps text.

For IMU section: a "signal path" horizontal 4-step diagram (sensores → registro → análisis → comparación) plus an illustrative chart SVG (three lines: orientación, inclinación) labeled "Ejemplo ilustrativo — no son datos de ensayo".

Let's write. Time 02:35. Must be done by 02:41. Writing ~3 big files takes a few minutes; verify at 02:40.

Go: styles.css.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
